{
  "_": [
    "Known-answer vectors for PBKDF2.",
    "",
    "`rfc6070Sha1` is RFC 6070 verbatim (PBKDF2-HMAC-SHA1). We do not ship SHA-1 anywhere; these run",
    "against the platform's WebCrypto directly, as a sanity check that the PBKDF2 implementation we",
    "are trusting is the one the RFC describes. RFC 6070's fourth vector (c = 16,777,216) is omitted:",
    "it is minutes of CPU for no additional signal.",
    "",
    "`sha256` is the widely-published PBKDF2-HMAC-SHA256 counterpart of the same inputs, and is what",
    "`pbkdf2Sha256` in src/crypto/kdf.ts is tested against.",
    "",
    "`p` and `s` are UTF-8 strings (\\u0000 appears deliberately in the last vector of each set);",
    "`c` is the iteration count, `dkLen` the output length in bytes, `dk` the expected output in hex."
  ],
